<http://data.silknow.org/object/069acea8-5ec8-30f7-a592-f7170255e4f8/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "A pair of abutted spheres showing the eastern and western hemispheres as they appeared between Cook's voyages and the Louisiana Purchase (1769-1803). Title is placed at the center top, the directional star at the center bottom. Each country and its colonies are delineated in a particular color. Soiled; some worn yarns; edges of ground partially frayed.  Stitches: couching, running, stem."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/069acea8-5ec8-30f7-a592-f7170255e4f8> .

